A voice box is a small wooden box about the size of a baseball, most of its sides plain unfinished wood, with a grate on the front like a speaker and a small button on one side beside it. The [[Org/Friends of Aut|Friends of Aut]] keep a shelf of them in the threshold room of the [[Pharos]] and let each group take one before crossing into the [[Geography/Black and White/index|Black and White]]. The box does not resonate. It is part of the ritual of that place: sounds are caught and put somewhere else with it. It grows warm near a sound worth catching.

Held near a caught sound and clicked, the box draws the sound in with a burst of moth wing scales, and a light on the side opposite the button comes on while the sound plays faintly from the grate. Poured into a speaker on one of the plaza buildings, a caught sound turns the building back to its working state and the light goes out. The box carries up to three sounds at once.
